"""Auto-generated interceptor verification for Hearthstone CORE.

Tests every card with a battlecry / deathrattle / setup_interceptors /
spell_effect in:
  - basic.py
  - classic.py
  - heroes.py + hero_powers.py
  - tokens.py
  - druid.py / hunter.py / mage.py / paladin.py / priest.py /
    rogue.py / shaman.py / warlock.py / warrior.py

Excluded by scope: frierenrift.py / riftclash.py / stormrift.py
(covered by a separate /test-interceptors agent).

Generated by /test-interceptors. Do NOT hand-edit — re-run the skill
if the card pool changes.

A test PASSES when, after firing the card's wired trigger, at least one
of these happens:
  1. The effect_fn returns events of an expected EventType (parsed from
     the card's rules text).
  2. A new interceptor was registered on game.state.interceptors
     (passives, auras, static lords).
  3. State directly mutated (mana_crystals_available, armor, weapon_attack)
     for cards that bypass the event pipeline.
  4. A PendingChoice was stashed on state.pending_choice (target-choice
     cards on the human path).

A test FAILS LOUDLY with "ENGINE GAP" prefix when the trigger fires but
the effect_fn returns [] and the rules text claims a concrete effect.
This is the depths trap the skill catches.
"""

